The visited set makes the count independent of discovery
order, sharing, and cycles. With hashed visited entries the
scan is expected linear in the reachable graph plus the
root list. Report the denominator as well as the fraction;
when $n=0$ the fraction is undefined, not zero locality.
Hold the retained graph and page size fixed when comparing
placements, and collect a separate access trace before making
claims about paging behavior.
